div.p:
13. But the ill consequences of even this species of schism do not terminate in the heart. Evil tempers cannot long remain within before they are productive of outward fruit. Out of the abundance of the heart the mouth speaketh.
Matt. 12:34. As he whose heart is full of love openeth his mouth with wisdom, and in his lips there is the law of kindness;
See Prov. 31:26. so he whose heart is full of prejudice, anger, suspicion, or any unkind temper, will surely open his mouth in a manner corresponding with the disposition of his mind. And hence will arise, if not lying and slandering (which yet will hardly be avoided), bitter words, talebearing, backbiting, and evil-speaking of every kind.
